{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1118703-technocracy-converted-akashic","id":1118703,"title":"Technocracy-converted Akashic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T14:37:03-07:00","id":1118703,"title":"Technocracy-converted Akashic","content":"Hey folks, <br /> I've just been thinking about the first antagonist my players are up against - she's not been in combat yet but may well be next session. <br /> I got to thinking, does an Akashic who is converted to the NWO paradigm retain the ability to use Do? Not as a focus, but it is described as being a little mystical, so I found myself thinking, does it just become brawl or martial arts instead? <br /> Can come up with my own answer if course but I wondered if anyone else had an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:02:22-07:00","id":1118787,"title":"","content":"If they had Do beforehand, they probably should still be able to use it as a Technocrat. It can be taught outside the Tradition to allies, and even Sleepers can even independently discover it; so I don't personally see any hard reason that they couldn't keep the Do they already have. The real reason it's not available outside the Akashayana seems to be that they're extremely cagey and possessive of it, much like the Tremere are with Thaumaturgy. <i>Increasing</i> it would be another matter, since they're tremendously unlikely to find anyone to teach them; advancing would require recreating deeper understanding from scratch.<br /> <br /> (I do recall a forum quest which included a character option of an Iterator Biomechanic who reverse-engineered Do via <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biomechanics\" target=\"_blank\">biomechanics</a> and used it as his focus, though not for any of the blatant vitalism stuff that the Akashics do like ki attacks. The character wasn't actually picked, but the idea was an interesting one. Naturally, he had as a flaw that he was continually hounded by ninjas.)<br /> <br /> The character will probably need to reinterpret it through the lens of their new paradigm to apply their Enlightenment to it in any useful ways, or to possibly teach it to others. They'll also probably not be able to get away with some of the more blatant displays of martial prowess just anywhere; that's more a political thing than a practical one, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 07-20-2017, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:05:55-07:00","id":1118789,"title":"","content":"Also, there are plenty of secret-agent martial arts tropes out there. Do would not be allowed, as it's a wrong paradigm and this is the NWO, but a martial artist with superb training can certainly break bricks, hit people at points on their body scientifically known to be vulnerable, and do parkour stunts.<br /> <br /> I'd probably make Do into Martial Arts, as Brawl is much less refined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T20:36:17-07:00","id":1118817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1118703-technocracy-converted-akashic?p=1118789#post1118789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there are plenty of secret-agent martial arts tropes out there. Do would not be allowed, as it's a wrong paradigm and this is the NWO, but a martial artist with superb training can certainly break bricks, hit people at points on their body scientifically known to be vulnerable, and do parkour stunts.<br /> <br /> I'd probably make Do into Martial Arts, as Brawl is much less refined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Do isn't just a martial art, it's a <i>life-style</i>. It's a philosophy. One can't examine Do in absence of Focus, because Do is intrinsically linked to a mystical Paradigm. You have to learn several other abilities to learn and advance in it.<br /> <br /> If an Akashic were turned Technocrat, their understanding of Do would rapidly degrade. Most likely devolving into a &quot;mere&quot; Martial Art. The old teachings and thought processes are no longer acceptable to the mage's Conditioned mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T00:47:38-07:00","id":1118859,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to turn it into &quot;ordinary&quot; martial arts then as they can fit within a technomantic paradigm, while do is a paradigm all of its own. <br /> Does anyone know where I can find rules? I have a lot of revised books and haven't found it yet in my research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T11:31:36-07:00","id":1119044,"title":"","content":"Try M20, page 566 for the table of good paradigm stuff and pages 580-581 for details on martial arts as a practice. M20 uses a paradigm, practices and instruments model. Practices are what is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T11:52:39-07:00","id":1119049,"title":"","content":"Cheers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13680_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13680\" data-vbnamecard=\"13680\">baakyocalder</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}